e Go backend only, following float-build's JS implementation as the reference. One backend, one commit.\n  kind: build\n  needs: [float-build]\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: float-build-lua\n  issue: gh:149\n  title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) for the Lua backend only (host hook), following float-build's JS implementation as the reference. One backend, one commit.\n  kind: build\n  needs: [float-build]\n  status: todo\n\n- id: float-build-jq\n  issue: gh:149\n  title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) for the jq backend only, following float-build's JS implementation as the reference. One backend, one commit.\n  kind: build\n  needs: [float-build]\n  status: todo\n\n- id: float-build-c-escalation\n  issue: gh:149\n  title: Attempt Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) for the C/LLVM backend; if there is no usable native matching primitive, write ESCALATION.md scoped to just this backend, commit it, and stop rather than stalling.\n  kind: build\n  needs: [float-build]","lineStart":95,"lineEnd":134,"totalLines":422,"truncated":true}},"title":"plans/board.yaml","time":{"start":1788373504305,"end":1788373504322}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The issue \"float-build-go\" is a board lane, not a GitHub issue. The GitHub issue is #149. The task says \"GitHub issue #float-build-go\" but gh issue view float-build-go fails because the GitHub issue is actually #149 (Implement Float). Let me look at the board to understand the lane.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0635e0de2001VYDg1rzDn24RAA","sessionID":"ses_f9ca2427bffeVwNvwc6e496rx3","messageID":"msg_0635e04cf001BU4ONrVf6rrEE8"}}
