{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788373512989,"sessionID":"ses_f9ca2427bffeVwNvwc6e496rx3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-81bb4092db994510","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-go/src","pattern":"Float"},"output":"Found 70 matches\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-go/src/ast.rs:\n  Line 221:     /// representation every JavaScript engine carries. The dot is what makes a number a Float,\n\n  Line 223:     Float {\n\n  Line 418:             | Expr::Float { span, .. }\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-go/src/ty.rs:\n  Line 29:     /// Float, and mixing the two in one operator is an error rather than a silent promotion.\n\n  Line 30:     /// Unlike the integer widths, arithmetic on a Float is total -- division by zero returns\n\n  Line 33:     Float,\n\n  Line 116:             \"Float\" => Some(Type::Float),\n\n  Line 278:             Type::Float => \"Float\".to_string(),\n\n  Line 319:             Type::Float => write!(f, \"Float\"),\n\n  Line 359:             | (Type::Float, Type::Float)\n\n  Line 417:         Type::Str | Type::Int | Type::Int64 | Type::Float | Type::Bool | Type::Char | Type::Sink => {\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-go/src/tir.rs:\n  Line 31:     /// in the node's own type -- there is only one float width, so a `Float` node is always\n\n  Line 33:     Float(f64),\n\n  Line 528:         | Kind::Float(_)\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-go/src/tags.rs:\n  Line 35:         | Kind::Float(_)\n\n  Line 116:         Kind::Float(_) => \"float\".into(),\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-go/src/emit_llvm.rs:\n  Line 342:             Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n\n  Line 444:             Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n\n  Line 463:             Type::Flo